course: dictionary
lesson: 5427
title: Lagomorphs: rabbits, hares and their teeth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lagomorph is a member of the group of mammals that includes rabbits, hares and pikas. Lagomorph is a noun, so you can talk about one lagomorph or many lagomorphs.
explain: Lagomorphs look a lot like rodents, such as mice and squirrels, but scientists put them in a separate group. The clue is in the teeth: lagomorphs have a small pair of upper front teeth hidden behind the big pair, while rodents have just one pair of big upper front teeth.
explain: «Rabbits and hares are not rodents but lagomorphs.» The sentence tells you that rabbits and hares belong to the lagomorph group. Lagomorphs and rodents are different groups, even though they can look alike.
fact: A lagomorph is a mammal in the group that includes rabbits, hares and pikas.
fact: Lagomorphs have four upper front teeth: a big pair at the front and a small pair hidden behind them.
fact: Rodents have one pair of big upper front teeth, so they do not have the small pair behind.
fact: Lagomorphs eat plants and often eat some of their droppings, which helps them digest their food twice.
fact: «Lagomorphs and rodents» are two different groups, even though they can look alike.
exercise: What is a lagomorph? | *A mammal group that includes rabbits, hares and pikas | A kind of plant that grows on hills | A type of bird that cannot fly
exercise: «Rabbits and hares are not rodents but lagomorphs.» Which animals are lagomorphs? | Mice and rats | Snakes and lizards | *Rabbits and hares
exercise: What helps you tell a lagomorph from a rodent? | Rodents have a small pair behind the big pair | Lagomorphs have wings | *A small pair of upper front teeth hidden behind the big pair | Lagomorphs have no front teeth at all
test: Which group does a pika belong to? | Rodents | Reptiles | Birds | *Lagomorphs
test: Why might a lagomorph eat some of its droppings? | To keep warm in winter | *To digest its food a second time | To hide from predators | To make its fur shiny
exam: Which feature shows a rabbit is a lagomorph and not a rodent? | It has a long, bare tail with no fur | It eats only meat | It has no front teeth at all | *It has a small pair of upper front teeth hidden behind the big pair
